  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in West Virginia totaled $1.1B in FY2026 to date. Contract activity includes 3,582 awards with an average award size of $309K. Obligations are down 41.0% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date), so the $1.1B figure does not represent a full fiscal year. Year-to-year history shows obligations of $1.5B in FY21, $1.5B in FY22, $1.7B in FY23, $2B in FY24, and $1.9B in FY25. Other notable FY2026 to date concentrations include $158M in Other Computer Related Services and $137M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology). The Department of Energy, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Justice are the largest buyers so far this year. LEIDOS, INC. is the top vendor by obligations in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal contracting in West Virginia change in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 41.0% year over year. FY2026 to date obligations total $1.1B, compared with $1.9B in FY25 and $2B in FY24. Award volume stands at 3,582 with an average award size of $309K. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and industries in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Justice are the top three buying agencies, with $230M, $213M, and $200M in obligations respectively. Other large buyers include the Department of Defense with $138M and the Department of the Treasury with $134M. Other Computer Related Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences are the top industries with $158M and $137M respectively. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction follows with $118M."
      }
    ]
  },
